: IDS/IPS Configuration (Snort and Suricata)
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Install and configure Snort and Suricata IDS/IPS systems
Create custom detection rules using Python scripting
Generate test traffic to validate IDS functionality
Analyze security alerts using the Elastic Stack (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana)
Compare Snort and Suricata capabilities and performance
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command line proficiency
Understanding of TCP/IP networking and common protocols
Familiarity with network security concepts
Basic Python programming skills
Knowledge of regular expressions
Lab Environment
Cloud Environment: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Ubuntu 22.04 LTS cloud machines. Click Start Lab to access your environment.

System Specifications:

Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
4GB RAM minimum
20GB disk space
Internet connectivity
Task 1: Install and Configure Snort and Suricata
Step 1.1: Install System Dependencies
Update your system and install required packages:

# Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install dependencies
sudo apt install -y build-essential libpcap-dev libpcre3-dev \
libdumbnet-dev bison flex zlib1g-dev liblzma-dev openssl \
libssl-dev pkg-config git wget curl python3 python3-pip \
libjansson-dev libnetfilter-queue-dev libhyperscan-dev
Step 1.2: Install Snort 3
# Create working directory
mkdir -p ~/ids-lab && cd ~/ids-lab

# Install libdaq
wget https://github.com/snort3/libdaq/archive/refs/tags/v3.0.11.tar.gz
tar -xzf v3.0.11.tar.gz
cd libdaq-3.0.11
./bootstrap && ./configure && make -j$(nproc)
sudo make install
cd ..

# Install Snort 3
wget https://github.com/snort3/snort3/archive/refs/tags/3.1.64.0.tar.gz
tar -xzf 3.1.64.0.tar.gz
cd snort3-3.1.64.0
./configure_cmake.sh --prefix=/usr/local
cd build && make -j$(nproc)
sudo make install
sudo ldconfig

# Verify installation
/usr/local/bin/snort --version
Step 1.3: Install Suricata
# Add Suricata repository
sudo add-apt-repository ppa:oisf/suricata-stable -y
sudo apt update

# Install Suricata
sudo apt install -y suricata

# Verify installation
suricata --version
Step 1.4: Create Directory Structure
# Snort directories
sudo mkdir -p /usr/local/etc/snort/{rules,so_rules,lists,preproc_rules}
sudo mkdir -p /var/log/snort

# Suricata directories
sudo mkdir -p /var/log/suricata
sudo mkdir -p /etc/suricata/rules

# Set permissions
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER /var/log/snort /var/log/suricata
Step 1.5: Configure Snort
Create basic Snort configuration:

sudo tee /usr/local/etc/snort/snort.lua > /dev/null << 'EOF'
-- Snort 3 Configuration
HOME_NET = '192.168.1.0/24'
EXTERNAL_NET = '!$HOME_NET'

daq = {
    inputs = { 'eth0' },
    snaplen = 1518,
}

stream = { }
http_inspect = { }

alert_fast = {
    file = '/var/log/snort/alert.txt',
}

ips = {
    rules = [[
        include /usr/local/etc/snort/rules/local.rules
        include /usr/local/etc/snort/rules/custom.rules
    ]]
}
EOF
